{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_result_unhandled_2.march","start_line":9,"start_col":15,"end_line":9,"end_col":25,"message":"This capability operation returns `Result((), CapError)`, which says whether it was permitted, but `()` is expected here.","code":"cap_result_unhandled","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":9,"start_col":15,"end_line":9,"end_col":25,"text":"Authority.ignore(println(v))","applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":["Handle the refusal (`match`, `let?`), or discard the result: a call on a line of its own needs nothing, and `Authority.ignore(...)` discards it anywhere else."],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
